{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockservicereference"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockServiceReference","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" is an actor that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" and records every call it receives. Use it in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#Preview"},{"type":"text","text":" blocks (where you don’t want real network traffic) and in tests (where you want deterministic assertions on what the plugin dispatched)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It does not import the Mixpanel SDK, so previews compile against it without configuring Mixpanel."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For usage examples, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Types","anchor":"Types","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"text":"``doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService``","anchor":"docSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsdocumentationSwiduxMixpanelAnalyticsMockMixpanelAnalyticsService","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public actor MockMixpanelAnalyticsService: AnalyticsService {","    public init(optedOut: Bool = false)","","    public nonisolated var isOptedOut: Bool { get }","    public func setOptedOut(_ optedOut: Bool) async","","    public private(set) var trackedEvents: [AnalyticsEvent]","    public private(set) var identifyCalls: [IdentifyCall]","    public private(set) var aliasCalls: [AliasCall]","    public private(set) var resetCount: Int","    public private(set) var flushCount: Int","    public private(set) var optOutCount: Int","    public private(set) var optInCalls: [OptInCall]","","    public struct IdentifyCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(userID: String, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue] = [:])","        public let userID: String","        public let properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]","    }","","    public struct AliasCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(newID: String, previousID: String? = nil)","        public let newID: String","        public let previousID: String?","    }","","    public struct OptInCall: Sendable, Equatable {","        public init(distinctID: String? = nil, properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]? = nil)","        public let distinctID: String?","        public let properties: [String: AnalyticsValue]?","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Recorded state","anchor":"Recorded-state","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackedEvents"},{"type":"text","text":" — every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":" passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", in dispatch order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identifyCalls"},{"type":"text","text":" — every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(userID, properties)"},{"type":"text","text":" pair passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify(userID:properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aliasCalls"},{"type":"text","text":" — every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(newID, previousID)"},{"type":"text","text":" pair passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias(newID:previousID:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resetCount"},{"type":"text","text":" — number of times "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reset()"},{"type":"text","text":" was called."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flushCount"},{"type":"text","text":" — number of times "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" was called."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutCount"},{"type":"text","text":" — number of times "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" was called."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optInCalls"},{"type":"text","text":" — every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(distinctID, properties)"},{"type":"text","text":" pair passed to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optInTracking(distinctID:properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"type":"text","text":" — current opt-out state."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"type":"text","text":" is synchronous, like the real service’s. Every other accessor is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":", so wrap reads in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":". The record types have public initializers, so tests can build expected values: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(await mock.identifyCalls == [.init(userID: \"user-1\")])"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Consent","anchor":"Consent","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(optedOut:)"},{"type":"text","text":" stands in for the real service’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTrackingByDefault"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"setOptedOut(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" routes to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optOutTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"optInTracking()"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly as the real service does, so the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onConsentChange: { await service.setOptedOut($0) }"},{"type":"text","text":" wiring works against either. The mock sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isOptedOut"},{"type":"text","text":" at once and records every call; it does not model the real service’s idempotence (a repeated opt-in is recorded again)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Determinism","anchor":"Determinism","level":4,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mock holds no buffers and adds no latency: every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"track"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias"},{"type":"text","text":" records synchronously inside the actor. The plugin’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"type":"text","text":" is still the right sync point for test assertions, since it drains the plugin’s own fire-and-forget task counter before the mock is queried."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The mock records "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"everything"}]},{"type":"text","text":", including calls the real adapter drops — blank-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" and blank-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"newID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias"},{"type":"text","text":" calls (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference"},{"type":"text","text":"), and calls made while opted out. A recording mock should never lose history; assert consent and validity at the call site, not by the absence of records."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"API reference for ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — a recording ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"}],"title":"Mock Service Reference","role":"article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"article","references":{"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/HowToPreviewAndTest":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"How to Preview and Test","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/HowToPreviewAndTest","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/howtopreviewandtest","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive "},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from SwiftUI previews and Swift Testing suites without touching Mixpanel’s network."}],"role":"article"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","title":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Recording ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"text":" for previews and Swift Testing suites.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mockmixpanelanalyticsservice"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/ServiceReference":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — the Mixpanel-backed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsService"},{"type":"text","text":" conformer that the analytics plugin consumes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/servicereference","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/ServiceReference","title":"Service Reference","role":"article","kind":"article"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics":{"abstract":[{"text":"Mixpanel adapter for Swidux’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Owns the Mixpanel SDK on the app’s behalf — ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService(token:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mixpanel.initialize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" internally so apps never need to ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Mixpanel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Ships a recording mock for previews and tests.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","title":"SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/documentation/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics/MixpanelAnalyticsService":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformer that owns and forwards to a Mixpanel SDK","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelAnalyticsService"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService"}}}